WEBVTT

00:02.063 --> 00:05.828
[Extreme justice leads to extreme injustice.]

00:05.829 --> 00:11.929
[Extreme justice leads to extreme injustice.]
[Cicero, On Obligations]

00:29.849 --> 00:31.513
What's going to happen now?

00:39.076 --> 00:41.779
Make no mistake, this additional exam…

00:42.279 --> 00:46.372
was set up specifically
to facilitate your expulsion.

00:46.849 --> 00:51.318
It simply would have been no fun
to let things end like that.

00:51.857 --> 00:55.529
So I decided to use Class A's positive votes

00:55.724 --> 00:57.888
to keep you safe.

00:58.638 --> 01:00.372
Why did you choose Yamauchi?

01:02.607 --> 01:07.302
Do you recall how rude he was
to me at the training camp?

01:19.904 --> 01:21.755
He had it coming.

01:21.888 --> 01:23.568
Oh, hello there.

01:25.428 --> 01:29.536
I'm the acting chairman of
the board for the time being.

01:30.295 --> 01:32.247
My name is Tsukishiro.

03:06.279 --> 03:07.521
Tsukishiro…

03:08.248 --> 03:11.185
This is my first visit to this school.

03:11.614 --> 03:13.735
Could you direct me to the staff room?

03:14.928 --> 03:18.677
Your sense of direction is a little
lacking for an acting chairman.

03:19.959 --> 03:24.794
I thought perhaps you had seen us on the
security cameras and come to question us.

03:25.474 --> 03:27.738
What an interesting idea.

03:28.247 --> 03:31.474
If you're looking for the
staff room, it's in another…

03:39.594 --> 03:44.700
You don't quite live up to the reputation
that precedes you, Ayanokouji Kiyotaka.

03:46.045 --> 03:48.771
Aren't you going a little too far?

03:49.342 --> 03:53.779
I could have sworn you were
instructed to have him expelled.

03:54.732 --> 03:58.341
The school can't expel someone so blatantly,

03:59.122 --> 04:03.107
so I can't blame them for
entrusting me with such a thing.

04:03.982 --> 04:08.990
But do you think the acting chairman
can get away with such violence?

04:09.388 --> 04:10.740
Not to worry.

04:11.998 --> 04:15.365
The security footage has been replaced.

04:16.529 --> 04:18.661
I have a message from your father.

04:20.192 --> 04:23.365
He's had enough of letting
you play your little games.

04:23.709 --> 04:27.654
You are to return at once, he says.

04:28.763 --> 04:30.935
Blink twice if you agree.

04:36.779 --> 04:39.723
So you won't drop out willingly.

04:49.342 --> 04:54.372
I will officially take my position
at this school in April.

04:55.029 --> 04:56.200
I will see you then.

05:02.904 --> 05:06.075
It was a wise move not to
try and fail to fight back.

05:06.701 --> 05:09.544
We don't know what they might use the footage for.

05:10.045 --> 05:11.411
But, anyway, Sakayanagi…

05:12.482 --> 05:15.935
Let's have our official battle in the next exam.

05:18.318 --> 05:21.575
I didn't think you'd suggest it yourself.

05:22.178 --> 05:24.880
If he's going to start working here in April,

05:25.271 --> 05:29.146
I want to settle things clearly
before that, and be done with it.

05:29.365 --> 05:33.372
Very well. I'll be happy to take you on.

05:42.045 --> 05:46.747
I'd like to explain the exam
that will finish out the year.

05:47.935 --> 05:52.021
It will be an event selection exam,
and you'll compete using teamwork.

05:52.701 --> 05:56.411
Like the paper shuffle, classes will
face off against one another.

05:57.774 --> 06:01.716
You will begin by choosing
any ten events you'd like.

06:03.717 --> 06:06.697
Don't hesitate to ask if you have any questions…

06:06.721 --> 06:07.388
Ike.

06:08.428 --> 06:13.630
O-Oh, but… you're not gonna get mad
at me for speaking out of turn?

06:13.865 --> 06:18.677
At this point, something wouldn't feel
right without your frivolous interruptions.

06:19.209 --> 06:22.638
Then… could we just pick
rock, paper, scissors or something?

06:22.693 --> 06:23.958
Of course not, stupid.

06:23.983 --> 06:25.825
Fine, let's go with that for now.

06:26.333 --> 06:27.333
Seriously?

06:27.865 --> 06:28.825
I don't mind.

06:29.560 --> 06:34.458
Keep in mind that you cannot
select duplicate events.

06:36.013 --> 06:41.365
We cannot allow events prohibited by available
equipment, time of year, or class size, either.

06:41.725 --> 06:43.967
[Beer pong, roundnet, kronum, padel,
hurling, da cau, jai alai, wood cobra]
The same goes for unnecessarily obscure events.

06:43.968 --> 06:44.889
[Beer pong, roundnet, kronum, padel,
hurling, da cau, jai alai, wood cobra]

06:45.193 --> 06:45.920
Based on the subject, school staff
will provide questions.

06:45.921 --> 06:47.073
[History, Biology, Chemistry, Physics,
Japanese, English]
Based on the subject, school staff
will provide questions.

06:47.097 --> 06:49.387
[Chemistry, Japanese, English]
Based on the subject, school staff
will provide questions.

06:49.388 --> 06:50.154
[Chemistry, Japanese, English]

06:50.162 --> 06:54.841
The rules are up to you, as long as they
do not allow for the event to end in a draw.

06:55.451 --> 06:58.785
Your competing class will also
submit ten events of their own.

06:58.810 --> 07:00.693
This makes twenty events in total.

07:01.115 --> 07:03.154
We're doing a whole twenty events?!

07:03.263 --> 07:04.755
That's way too much!

07:05.092 --> 07:05.818
Don't worry.

07:06.560 --> 07:11.599
On the day of the exam, each class
will choose five of their proposed events.

07:12.441 --> 07:14.818
So the other five are just a bluff?

07:14.951 --> 07:15.673
Precisely.

07:15.697 --> 07:18.212
The actual exam will consist of seven rounds.

07:18.614 --> 07:22.301
For each round, the school will
randomly select one proposed event.

07:22.824 --> 07:26.331
There will be no indication of
what the next event will be.

07:26.395 --> 07:31.027
No student can participate a second time
until everyone has finished an event.

07:31.138 --> 07:33.825
I'm getting kind of confused over here…

07:33.959 --> 07:36.904
So, that means…

07:37.516 --> 07:39.857
Both classes propose events,

07:39.998 --> 07:43.372
and in the end, we compete in seven of them.

07:43.717 --> 07:45.365
Okay, got it.

07:45.794 --> 07:50.270
The most important rule concerns the leader.

07:51.240 --> 07:55.240
The student designated as leader
cannot compete in events,

07:55.568 --> 08:00.365
but can interfere in any of them, and
receives bonus points if their class wins.

08:01.021 --> 08:02.919
So, what if their class loses?

08:05.793 --> 08:08.177
The leader will be expelled immediately.

08:10.498 --> 08:11.795
Not this again!

08:12.209 --> 08:16.372
After school, the leader will select
an opponent class by lottery.

08:16.834 --> 08:18.185
The leader is up to you.

08:18.974 --> 08:20.545
Discuss it among yourselves.

08:23.099 --> 08:24.833
[Exam Overview]

08:25.365 --> 08:27.013
What happened to Kouenji?

08:27.756 --> 08:30.779
Damn Kouenji, he's blowing it off again!

08:30.844 --> 08:32.971
Don't waste your energy getting angry.

08:33.169 --> 08:35.505
Hey, where did Hirata go?

08:35.794 --> 08:39.207
I don't know. We were all
supposed to meet up after school.

08:39.678 --> 08:43.895
If Hirata is out of commission,
I suppose I'll have to do this myself.

08:45.817 --> 08:50.786
I, um, have to go to the bathroom
really quick! I'll be right back!

08:52.131 --> 08:53.021
Hey.

08:53.646 --> 08:56.794
Before we start discussin',
I got a question for you.

08:56.912 --> 08:57.747
What is it?

08:58.334 --> 09:02.208
A lot of people ain't happy with
the last exam's results.

09:02.553 --> 09:03.786
Right, Kanji?

09:04.013 --> 09:08.818
Well, I don't know if I'd say they're
not happy, but some people don't get it.

09:08.974 --> 09:12.818
Like, why was Ayanokouji in first place?

09:13.842 --> 09:16.029
Allow me to explain that.

09:16.443 --> 09:18.021
I've been thinking it over.

09:18.099 --> 09:18.997
Wait a minute.

09:19.349 --> 09:22.372
We want Ayanokouji to explain it himself.

09:22.630 --> 09:25.075
We lost a friend, you know.

09:25.607 --> 09:28.232
Sorry. I don't know why, either.

09:28.592 --> 09:30.427
Like hell you don't!

09:30.654 --> 09:33.169
I doubt Ayanokouji would have an answer.

09:33.412 --> 09:35.575
It was done behind his back.

09:35.732 --> 09:38.872
Behind his back… what d'you mean?

09:39.490 --> 09:41.950
Do you recall what Yamauchi said?

09:43.076 --> 09:48.263
Oh, right, all you have to do is ask Sakayanagi!
She promised me those votes!

09:48.615 --> 09:50.896
Is she allowed to just lie about it?!

09:52.607 --> 09:58.154
She put Yamauchi into motion with a secret promise
to take down Ayanokouji, and she betrayed him.

09:58.453 --> 10:01.351
But why Ayanokouji?

10:01.481 --> 10:05.714
She chose someone she could take or leave,
so the protection point is trivial.

10:05.739 --> 10:08.733
I'm sure it could've been
anyone meeting those criteria.

10:08.904 --> 10:11.638
Yeah, but… aren't you just guessing?

10:11.748 --> 10:13.365
Yes, this is conjecture.

10:14.935 --> 10:19.318
But if you want to blame someone,
blame me, not Ayanokouji.

10:19.826 --> 10:23.825
I'm the main reason Yamauchi was expelled.

10:24.592 --> 10:25.833
Well…

10:28.115 --> 10:32.630
Can I be considered for the
leader position for this exam?

10:32.935 --> 10:33.615
Huh?

10:34.255 --> 10:37.060
I can't deny that everyone's suspicious of me now.

10:37.771 --> 10:42.240
So I want to clear up those doubts by
putting myself on the chopping block.

10:42.678 --> 10:43.732
Ayanokouji…

10:43.763 --> 10:47.605
That works! Then we can get through it
without anyone being expelled!

10:47.630 --> 10:52.731
Hey, wait a minute! Isn't that just
throwing in the towel from the start?

10:53.271 --> 10:56.958
Do we stand any chance as a class
with Ayanokouji directing us?

10:57.053 --> 11:00.310
Shouldn't we at least consider other people, too?

11:01.842 --> 11:02.271
Huh?

11:02.826 --> 11:08.404
I don't think anyone here is willing to
risk expulsion. Myself included.

11:08.974 --> 11:10.630
Guess you're right.

11:10.717 --> 11:14.083
Isn't he the clear choice, since he
has a protection point?

11:15.849 --> 11:20.700
Even if he's the leader, someone else
can still plan out a strategy beforehand.

11:21.396 --> 11:23.716
It doesn't matter much who the leader is.

11:24.724 --> 11:28.474
Horikita is putting the leadership
completely in my hands.

11:28.865 --> 11:32.333
I doubt anyone has a mind
to argue at this point, either.

11:32.592 --> 11:34.302
Any further objections?

11:38.192 --> 11:42.677
Very well, Ayanokouji. Can I ask you
to go draw our opponent?

11:43.279 --> 11:44.279
On it.

11:49.138 --> 11:55.068
I guess all the other classes made the person
with the protection point their leader, too.

11:56.115 --> 11:59.552
You will each draw once.

11:59.967 --> 12:05.255
The one who draws the winning card will win
the right to choose an opponent for their class.

12:06.013 --> 12:08.888
They say one man's trash
is another man's treasure,

12:09.178 --> 12:11.271
so I don't mind going last.

12:11.693 --> 12:13.075
Go ahead, Ichinose.

12:13.545 --> 12:15.544
Alright, don't mind if I do.

12:21.365 --> 12:22.599
Too bad!

12:24.435 --> 12:26.270
[Opponent Class Selection Ticket]

12:26.513 --> 12:27.661
Looks like I win.

12:28.178 --> 12:33.021
I suppose there's no need to look
at the last one, Mr. Mashima.

12:33.427 --> 12:33.998
Right.

12:34.756 --> 12:38.427
Well, Kaneda, which class would you
like to compete against?

12:38.982 --> 12:42.482
Class D will be competing against Class B.

12:42.623 --> 12:45.083
Okay, let's give it all we've got.

12:45.584 --> 12:48.966
I thought surely you had
your sights set on Class C.

12:49.240 --> 12:54.411
Going after a class with more points might be
a good way to turn things around in the future,

12:54.615 --> 12:57.677
but I'd rather avoid competing
with Class A for now.

12:58.435 --> 13:02.177
Very well. I wish you all the best.

13:03.209 --> 13:04.795
It's the obvious result.

13:05.967 --> 13:10.349
Ichinose and Ishizaki set this up in advance.

13:12.506 --> 13:13.506
[Ishizaki Daichi]
[Understood!]

13:14.896 --> 13:18.740
So that we'd be the ones going up against Class A.

13:19.966 --> 13:24.971
[Classroom of the Elite
3rd Season]

13:27.381 --> 13:28.904
That's all for today.

13:29.537 --> 13:31.841
It's over, I'm finally free!

13:38.872 --> 13:40.060
Hirata!

13:41.037 --> 13:42.833
We're going to discuss…

13:43.303 --> 13:45.279
Can't you just leave me alone?

13:45.357 --> 13:46.200
But…

13:46.225 --> 13:47.787
You're getting on my nerves!

13:51.373 --> 13:54.325
I… I just, um…

13:54.803 --> 13:58.318
I'm just a little worried about you…

13:58.513 --> 14:00.833
It's no concern of yours.

14:01.873 --> 14:06.075
Hey, Yousuke! Don't you think
you're being a little harsh?

14:06.833 --> 14:09.739
Can you stop using my
first name like we're close?

14:10.279 --> 14:12.474
You have nothing to do with me anymore.

14:12.724 --> 14:16.043
Fine, then, Hirata.
You're being too harsh with Mii.

14:16.076 --> 14:18.857
I'm not acting any differently than you always do.

14:19.592 --> 14:21.755
I-I'm just looking out for the class!

14:21.858 --> 14:23.997
Can you just stop talking now?

14:24.388 --> 14:25.388
I'm sure you know…

14:26.020 --> 14:27.481
what happens if you don't.

14:39.459 --> 14:41.505
Wait, Hirata!

14:45.099 --> 14:48.122
There's nothing we can do about Hirata right now.

14:48.607 --> 14:50.865
Let's focus on the task at hand.

14:51.748 --> 14:55.240
By the way, Kouenji, you bothered
to stick around for once?

14:56.771 --> 14:59.732
My girl Horikita here wouldn't
take no for an answer.

15:01.185 --> 15:06.029
However, I'd like to get all of
our discussion done in one go.

15:06.162 --> 15:07.919
I'm very busy, you see.

15:08.326 --> 15:09.896
I'll be brief, then.

15:10.279 --> 15:15.466
When I see you next, I'd like you all to have any
event you know you can win written down.

15:15.904 --> 15:21.919
So I see. You want me to not only participate in
the discussion, but win an event as well, do you?

15:22.435 --> 15:25.279
I'm sure there's something you know you can win.

15:25.560 --> 15:28.497
Or are you fine with the class writing you off?

15:29.560 --> 15:33.794
Don't get in your head that you can
force my hand with such words.

15:34.295 --> 15:37.646
I do indeed have an ability
in which I am unrivaled,

15:38.467 --> 15:43.200
but it's my choice whether or not
to use that ability for your benefit.

15:45.361 --> 15:48.068
What the hell are you unrivaled in?

15:48.553 --> 15:53.005
I'll try talking to him later.
Let's wait and see for now.

16:02.482 --> 16:03.482
Um, hey.

16:04.849 --> 16:08.747
It's not every day you invite me to your room.

16:09.795 --> 16:11.860
What if someone sees me here?

16:12.368 --> 16:15.435
Like, wouldn't that be bad for you?

16:15.670 --> 16:18.482
There's less need to hide it now.

16:20.060 --> 16:24.693
I guess we're being more open
about our whole thing now…

16:25.474 --> 16:26.591
That's not an issue?

16:27.061 --> 16:28.529
No issue at all.

16:28.857 --> 16:32.247
Hirata is a concern. I need to
know what the class is saying.

16:32.513 --> 16:35.966
So like, is that something that
has to be discussed in person?

16:36.365 --> 16:40.154
There are some things you understand
best from talking face-to-face.

16:40.678 --> 16:41.678
Hmm…

16:42.013 --> 16:43.497
But first of all…

16:49.097 --> 16:49.880
Huh?

16:50.161 --> 16:52.333
Today's your birthday, right?

16:53.404 --> 16:57.333
I didn't know you knew! Can I open it now?

16:57.607 --> 16:58.216
Yeah.

17:00.576 --> 17:01.326
Whoa!

17:02.217 --> 17:03.536
A necklace?!

17:04.310 --> 17:06.208
Wait, it's heart-shaped!

17:06.739 --> 17:09.465
Is it normal to give a friend this kind of thing?

17:10.506 --> 17:12.505
Aren't these pretty expensive?

17:12.717 --> 17:14.060
I guess it wasn't cheap.

17:14.473 --> 17:15.973
Around 20,000 points or so.

17:16.131 --> 17:17.131
That's a lot!

17:17.318 --> 17:23.208
I just bought the thing on the online store that
was ranked #1 in birthday presents for girls.

17:23.740 --> 17:27.715
For someone so smart,
you're really stupid sometimes.

17:28.295 --> 17:29.466
You think so?

17:29.623 --> 17:33.482
Girls like picking out their own accessories!

17:34.021 --> 17:37.794
Just so you know, this is like a 10/100 present.

17:38.451 --> 17:40.458
Should I have gotten a cake instead?

17:41.545 --> 17:43.224
That'd be a 15.

17:46.786 --> 17:47.974
Do you have a mirror?

17:48.178 --> 17:49.599
Do I look like I would?

17:53.123 --> 17:57.433
Yeah, I think heart-shaped necklaces
are really more of a kid thing.

17:58.013 --> 18:00.403
If you don't want it, I can just return it.

18:00.513 --> 18:05.560
I'm a high-value woman, though,
so everything looks good on me.

18:08.154 --> 18:10.396
I'll be nice and take it off your hands.

18:10.497 --> 18:12.661
Okay, that's a relief, I guess.

18:18.873 --> 18:23.482
[Pedestrian and Bicycle Crossing]

18:25.904 --> 18:26.904
You're early.

18:27.123 --> 18:29.458
I need to stop by the library.

18:30.092 --> 18:31.092
I see.

18:31.795 --> 18:33.927
Are you prepared for the exam?

18:34.428 --> 18:37.185
Your sister is putting in the work for me.

18:37.717 --> 18:38.717
Interesting.

18:39.365 --> 18:43.029
Speaking of which, there's something
I've been wanting to ask you.

18:44.201 --> 18:46.286
On the day we first met,

18:47.271 --> 18:50.607
why did you tear into her
and try to get her to leave?

18:54.365 --> 18:56.529
I was disappointed in her.

18:57.092 --> 19:00.435
Not in her academic achievements,
but in her personal growth.

19:00.607 --> 19:02.388
Her personal growth?

19:02.700 --> 19:05.497
She smiled much more as a child.

19:05.912 --> 19:10.536
Now, all she does is depend
on me, and copy what I do.

19:11.490 --> 19:16.286
So you're saying that her cool and collected act
is something she got from you?

19:16.482 --> 19:18.029
It's not just her attitude.

19:18.318 --> 19:23.060
What she eats, what she drinks, her
favorite color, even the way she dresses.

19:23.513 --> 19:26.146
All of it is in pursuit of my preferences.

19:26.717 --> 19:28.521
That isn't growth at all.

19:29.185 --> 19:35.294
You seem so perfect, but you still fail at
communicating with your sister?

19:35.857 --> 19:39.286
No human is perfect. Do you disagree?

19:39.974 --> 19:41.169
You're right.

19:41.741 --> 19:45.099
But she's trying to change now.

19:45.739 --> 19:50.692
If Suzune stops chasing my shadow,
becomes independent,

19:51.037 --> 19:55.318
and can move forward being true to herself,

19:56.053 --> 20:01.005
she could surpass me, and become
impossible for you to ignore.

20:01.638 --> 20:04.240
Only if she is able to change, however.

20:05.935 --> 20:07.435
Don't you think she will?

20:08.334 --> 20:10.068
No, more like…

20:10.748 --> 20:12.810
I'm going to change her.

20:13.513 --> 20:16.118
Not passively like I have so far.

20:16.142 --> 20:17.568
Deliberately.

20:18.678 --> 20:21.747
Oh? I didn't expect to hear such a thing from you.

20:22.121 --> 20:24.012
There's just one more problem.

20:24.475 --> 20:25.255
What?

20:25.779 --> 20:29.216
Are you dating Tachibana?

20:30.497 --> 20:32.715
No, nothing of the sort.

20:33.474 --> 20:34.247
Okay.

20:35.951 --> 20:41.529
But it's interesting to hear you ask.
You sound like an ordinary high-schooler.

20:42.021 --> 20:45.677
I'm pretty sure I'm the most
ordinary high-schooler there is.

20:46.068 --> 20:50.411
Do you have a girlfriend, then,
Mr. Ordinary High-Schooler?

20:50.834 --> 20:52.669
Not so far, no.

20:53.592 --> 20:56.818
I trust you to reassure Suzune,

20:57.537 --> 21:00.036
but that's one thing I cannot picture.

21:00.349 --> 21:01.568
Well, obviously.

21:01.811 --> 21:03.450
D-Don't say that!

21:03.873 --> 21:06.544
You're going to jinx it!

21:06.646 --> 21:07.427
Jinx it?

21:07.615 --> 21:08.333
Um…

21:08.639 --> 21:09.841
Well, I mean…

21:10.076 --> 21:13.396
It's like reverse psychology…

21:13.630 --> 21:17.318
You always hear about people saying
they'll never end up together,

21:17.537 --> 21:20.107
but then they do.

21:21.717 --> 21:24.544
N-Never mind, forget it!

21:25.950 --> 21:29.379
[Chess, Mental Arithmetic, Go, Modern Japanese,
Mathematics, English, Jump Rope, Dodgeball]

21:29.740 --> 21:32.341
These are the events Class A has proposed.

21:32.460 --> 21:35.450
We're gonna have a hard time
countering all of these!

21:35.670 --> 21:39.115
Yes. But Class A will be in the same position.

21:39.599 --> 21:43.068
Our next challenge is to narrow down
the best of our choices.

21:43.373 --> 21:46.333
Does anyone here even play chess?

21:47.131 --> 21:47.974
Chess…

